# November 22, 2026: Louisville, Kentucky. A "videos" session (PROMPTS.md job 9): the names came from one video's tour of
# old Louisville buildings (the record is source/videos/20230703_o0OVZh9H_JM.md); the video is a tip and nothing here
# rests on it. Sources read in this session: Wikipedia (each article named in the links), the Kentucky Historical
# Society's marker pages (City Hall, St. Joseph, St. Boniface), the National Register form for the Louisville Trust
# Building (NPGallery text), Louisville Public Media (June 2025) on Louisville Gardens, and the own pages of Louisville
# Water (Water Tower and WaterWorks Museum), the Kentucky Derby Museum and St. Boniface parish for hours. Pins are
# address lookups (ArcGIS PointAddress) or the Register list point, each looked at on the aerial. Interiors were not
# visited by any source opened unless the entry says so.
